  "question": "This backend system is designed for managing work order processing information across different support departments.\n1.Department Management:The system allows you to create, modify, and delete different support departments. For each department, you can set:\nDepartment name, description, and email address.Sorting order. Whether the department only allows customers to submit work orders.Whether work orders are only responded to via email pipeline.Whether auto-replies are disabled.Whether the department is hidden from users.\n2.Email Configuration:For each department, configure the email server’s host address, port number, login username, and password, allowing the system to automatically handle emails.\n3.Employee Email Server Maintenance:\nEmployees can maintain the email server in real-time.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0488\nCREATE TABLE `departments` (\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `department_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email_address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `sort_order` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `customer_only` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `email_pipeline_only` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `disable_auto_reply` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `hidden_from_users` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  PRIMARY KEY (`department_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `department_email_config` (\n  `config_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `host_address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `port_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `login_username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `login_password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`config_id`),\n  KEY `department_email_config_ibfk_1` (`department_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `department_email_config_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`department_id`) REFERENCES `departments` (`department_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employee_email_servers` (\n  `server_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `employee_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `server_host` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `server_port` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `server_username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `server_password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`server_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
